<li>Farms near national parks and protected forest in Lampung, Bengkulu and South Sumatra</li>
<li>Cherry and green bean bought through layers of collectors with no paper trail</li>
<li>Blending lots from many origins in the warehouse</li>
<li>Farmers without formal land certificates</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style="background: #006386; color: #FFFFFF; border-radius: 14px; padding: 22px">
<h3 style="font-size: 17px; font-weight: 700; color: #FFFFFF">What PasarMIKRO delivers</h3>
<ul style="margin: 12px 0 0; padding-left: 20px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.75; color: #F2F4F7">
<li>Plot point or polygon for every supplying farmer, captured in the field</li>
<li>Satellite screening against the 2020 forest baseline and protected areas</li>
<li>Each purchase recorded in the app, linking plot to collector to lot</li>
<li>Segregated, EUDR-ready lots and a data pack your buyer can file from</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section id="cocoa" style="padding: 0 0 96px">
<div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 20px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 48px">
<div style="flex: 1 1 420px; min-width: 0">
<div style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: #006386">Cocoa</div>
<h2 style="font-size: 38px; line-height: 1.12; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.025em; margin-top: 14px">EUDR for Indonesian cocoa: Sulawesi, Bali and beyond</h2>
<p style="font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.65; color: #475467; margin-top: 16px">Indonesian cocoa comes from smallholder gardens, often agroforestry, and moves through village traders before reaching fermenters, grinders and exporters. EUDR covers beans and every derived product your EU buyer makes from them, so the plot data has to survive processing.</p>
<img src={cocoaPole.src} alt="A farmer harvesting cocoa pods with a long pole under shade trees" style="display: block; width: 100%; height: 300px; object-fit: cover; object-position: center 40%; border-radius: 16px; margin-top: 28px">
