<p style="font-size: 15px; color: #475467; margin-top: 12px">Example scenarios showing how a typical engagement runs.</p>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 36px">
<div style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #EAECF0; border-radius: 16px; padding: 28px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<div style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; color: #006386">Robusta exporter · Lampung</div>
<h3 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.3">A German importer asks for plot data on next season's contract</h3>
<p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #475467"><strong style="color: #003143">Challenge:</strong> beans arrive through a dozen collectors; the exporter knows the collectors but not the farms.</p>
<p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #475467"><strong style="color: #003143">With PasarMIKRO:</strong> collectors onboard their farmers in the app, plots are mapped and screened, flagged farms near park boundaries are verified in the field, and compliant volume is bought and stored as separate lots.</p>
<p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #475467"><strong style="color: #003143">Result:</strong> each container ships with a data pack the importer files from.</p>
</div>
<div style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #EAECF0; border-radius: 16px; padding: 28px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<div style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; color: #006386">Cocoa cooperative · Sulawesi</div>
<h3 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.3">A cooperative risks losing its European grinder</h3>
<p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #475467"><strong style="color: #003143">Challenge:</strong> a member list on paper, no plot locations, and agroforestry gardens that satellites read as forest.</p>
<p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #475467"><strong style="color: #003143">With PasarMIKRO:</strong> a member and plot registry, field checks to document gardens established before 2021, and digital purchase records through fermentation.</p>
<p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #475467"><strong style="color: #003143">Result:</strong> the grinder receives evidence it can rely on, and members get faster payment.</p>
</div>
<div style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #EAECF0; border-radius: 16px; padding: 28px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<div style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; color: #006386">Specialty arabica · Java &amp; Bali</div>
<h3 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.3">A small exporter selling micro-lots to EU roasters</h3>
<p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #475467"><strong style="color: #003143">Challenge:</strong> many small lots, limited staff, and roasters each asking for data in a different format.</p>
<p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #475467"><strong style="color: #003143">With PasarMIKRO:</strong> lightweight onboarding with Mikro ERP, one standard data pack per lot, and origin stories roasters can use on the bag.</p>
<p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #475467"><strong style="color: #003143">Result:</strong> compliance becomes a selling point for specialty buyers.</p>
