<section id="faq" style="padding: 0 0 96px">
<div style="max-width: 880px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 20px">
<h2 style="font-size: 38px; line-height: 1.12; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.025em">EUDR questions from Indonesian exporters</h2>
<div style="margin-top: 32px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0">
<div style="border-top: 1px solid #EAECF0; padding: 22px 0"><h3 style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700">When does EUDR apply to Indonesian coffee and cocoa?</h3><p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; color: #475467; margin-top: 8px">From 30 December 2026 for large and medium companies placing products on the EU market, and from 30 June 2027 for micro and small companies. The European Commission confirmed in May 2026 that there will be no further postponement.</p></div>
<div style="border-top: 1px solid #EAECF0; padding: 22px 0"><h3 style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700">I export from Indonesia. Do I file the due diligence statement?</h3><p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; color: #475467; margin-top: 8px">Usually your EU importer files it, as the first company placing the goods on the EU market. But they can only do so with your plot geolocation, legality evidence and lot records, so in practice the data work sits with you.</p></div>
<div style="border-top: 1px solid #EAECF0; padding: 22px 0"><h3 style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700">What risk level is Indonesia?</h3><p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; color: #475467; margin-top: 8px">Standard risk. Operators must run full due diligence with risk assessment and mitigation, and EU authorities check at least 3% of operators sourcing from standard-risk countries.</p></div>
<div style="border-top: 1px solid #EAECF0; padding: 22px 0"><h3 style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700">Do smallholders need polygons?</h3><p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; color: #475467; margin-top: 8px">Plots of 4 hectares or less can be recorded as a single GPS point; plots over 4 hectares need a polygon of the boundary. Many buyers prefer polygons for all plots because they make deforestation checks more reliable.</p></div>
<div style="border-top: 1px solid #EAECF0; padding: 22px 0"><h3 style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700">Is a certification like Rainforest Alliance or Fairtrade enough?</h3><p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; color: #475467; margin-top: 8px">No. Certification helps with risk assessment, but EUDR still requires plot geolocation and a due diligence statement for every shipment.</p></div>
{offer && (<Fragment><div style="border-top: 1px solid #EAECF0; border-bottom: 1px solid #EAECF0; padding: 22px 0"><h3 style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700">What does the early-joiner offer include?</h3><p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; color: #475467; margin-top: 8px">Companies that sign up for the PasarMIKRO EUDR Program by 13 November 2026 get the EUDR consultation and the initial platform setup free of charge.</p></div></Fragment>)}
</div>
</div>
</section>

